# JSON-LD and structured data

- Structured data must describe visible, verified page content. It is not a place to publish draft company facts, unsupported rankings, hidden products, inferred ratings, or marketing guarantees.
- Select the most specific valid Schema.org types only after checking current Google documentation and Schema.org definitions. Do not assume `LocalBusiness`, `EducationalOrganization`, `SportsActivityLocation`, `Course`, or `Product` eligibility from the brand description alone.
- Type payloads with the project `JsonLdDocument` type. Keep builders in a server-safe shared/domain module and derive program/price fields from the same typed source as the visible UI.
- Give the organization a stable canonical `@id` based on the verified production origin and reuse it when relating the website, organization, place, services, and offers. Do not mint conflicting identities per component.
- Include address, telephone, opening hours, geo, `sameAs`, logos, images, price/availability, and track/location relationships only when each value is verified and publicly visible where appropriate.
- Starting prices must retain their qualifier in visible copy. Structured `Offer` values must use numeric `price` and ISO `priceCurrency`; do not encode `от 30 000 ₽` as an arbitrary price string or imply a final checkout price.
- Render JSON-LD with a native `<script type="application/ld+json">` in a Server Component. `next/script` is for executable scripts and is not needed for JSON-LD.
- Serialize through one safe helper that uses `JSON.stringify(payload).replace(/</g, "\\u003c")` so content cannot terminate the script tag. Never interpolate raw strings into JSON-LD markup.
- Do not accept user-provided or CMS HTML directly into JSON-LD. Validate/normalize external content at ingestion and still apply the safe serializer.
- Emit each entity once per page and compose a graph when relationships matter. Avoid duplicate organization blocks from layout, footer, and page components.
- JSON-LD must not create hydration work. It belongs in the server-rendered route/layout and must not be updated through effects.
- Validate final production markup with Schema Markup Validator and Google's Rich Results Test where the selected type is supported. Treat warnings according to the actual type; fix all factual or syntactic errors.
